ISSUE: rmdir of somebody's (even YOUR) current directory. I had initially
wanted to deny rmdir of a directory which is anybody's current directory on
that drive, because it's safer.  However, a current directory can be a
pretty wierd concept when even the guy who did it has forgotten about it. 
In addition, the Desktop actually does a chdir to a directory, then rmdir
of that same directory.  Therefore, rmdir has to allow deleting any  empty
directory, and we have to decide what to do.  Decision: bump them up to ..
rather than bumping them all the way to root, which is the only other
option.  (Bumping to root has precedent: it happens after media change.
However, that's the ONLY solution after media change, so that's no help.)

